{
  "title": "Prevent concurrent recipe writes from silently losing updates",
  "description": "Recipe updates read the current version, merge request \
fields into that snapshot, then use `create_new_version`, which \
unconditionally repoints `recipes.current_version_id`. Several enrichment and \
pipeline write paths use the same helper. Concurrent edits can both report \
success while the last pointer update silently replaces the other edit. \
Long-running AI operations make this especially likely. A compare-and-swap \
helper already exists for generated descriptions and photos, but it currently \
only supports copying tags.\n\
\n\
Scope:\n\
- Generalize the shared version-write path so compare-and-swap writes support \
all required TagSource strategies. Keep recipe/version/tag changes atomic.\n\
- Require ordinary update requests to identify the version they edited and \
return a typed 409 conflict when it is stale. Add API end-to-end tests before \
changing either client.\n\
- Update both web and iOS edit flows to submit the expected version and \
present the conflict without overwriting either version.\n\
- Audit normalize-title, auto-tag, generated-description, rescrape, and \
save-recipe pipeline writes. Any operation based on a snapshot must either use \
CAS or document and test why unconditional replacement is correct.\n\
- Add deterministic concurrency tests covering user-vs-user and \
user-vs-enrichment races.\n\
\n\
Do not retain the unconditional path merely for backwards compatibility; this \
project has no production compatibility requirement.",
  "status": "open",
  "priority": 1,
